# 1. Project Overview

## ✈️ The Problem

Planning a trip becomes more difficult when multiple people are involved.

Travellers may have different budgets, interests, travel pace, food preferences, transportation preferences and must-visit places. This makes group decision-making difficult, and one person often ends up doing most of the planning.

Solo travellers may face another problem: they want to travel but do not have a suitable travel companion because their friends may be unavailable, have different budgets or prefer different travel styles.

Travel plans can also become unsuitable when circumstances change. Bad weather, delays, tiredness, attraction closures, budget changes or changes in group members may require the group to revise the itinerary.

TripSync focuses on three connected problems:

- **Finding suitable people to travel with**
- **Helping a group reach agreement fairly**
- **Adapting the plan when circumstances change**

### Existing Solutions

Existing travel planning applications can already help users organize trips, create itineraries, manage reservations or collaborate with others.

However, TripSync focuses on a more connected group-travel experience:

- finding compatible travel companions
- understanding group preferences
- allowing members to vote together
- balancing different members fairly
- adapting the itinerary when something goes wrong

TripSync is therefore not designed only to answer:

> **"Where should we go?"**

It also considers:

> **"Who should I travel with?"**  
> **"How can everyone agree?"**  
> **"What happens when the plan changes?"**

---

## 💡 Our Solution

**TripSync** is an AI-powered group travel planner and travel teaming prototype.

The experience is built around:

> **Find → Agree → Plan → Adapt**

TripSync supports two main ways to start a trip.

### 🔎 Open Trip

For users who want to meet compatible travel companions.

An Open Trip can include:

- Destination
- Trip dates
- Minimum and maximum budget
- Transport preference
- Maximum members
- Travel styles
- Preferred traveller types

Examples of preferred traveller types:

- Students
- Young Adults
- Food Lovers
- Photographers
- Adventure Travellers
- Relaxed Travellers
- Budget Travellers

Open Trips are intended for public discovery.

### 🔒 Private Group

For users who already know who they want to travel with.

Current private group options include:

- Friends
- Family
- Couple
- School / Club
- Company / Team

Private Groups use invitation-based planning rather than public discovery.

---

## ⭐ Current Core Features

- 👥 Open Trip and Private Group creation
- 🔎 Public trip discovery
- 🧩 Travel Compatibility / Group Matching
- 🎭 Travel Personality and preference collection
- 👤 Friends and Travel Buddies invitation flow
- 🗳️ Activity voting with Must Go, Like, Neutral and Skip
- 📊 Voting progress
- ⚖️ Group Match and Fairness Meter
- 🤖 AI-generated activity suggestions
- 🤖 AI-generated final itinerary
- 🚨 Plan Rescue
- ❤️ People / Travel Buddies management
- 🧭 Five main app areas: Explore, My Trips, Plan, People and Profile

---

# 2. Ideation & Process

## 2.1 Ideas We Considered

Our team explored ideas across the full group travel journey.

We kept ideas that directly support TripSync's main experience:

> **Find → Agree → Plan → Adapt**

Features with higher technical complexity or weaker relevance to the MVP were moved to future development.

| **Idea** | **Why it was kept / dropped** |
|---|---|
| **Travel Teaming / Open Trips (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Helps users who want to travel but do not have suitable companions discover groups based on destination, budget and travel preferences. |
| **Private Groups (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Friends, families, couples, school/club groups and company teams can plan privately through invitations. |
| **Travel Compatibility (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Helps compare factors such as budget, interests, pace and transport preferences. |
| **Travel Personality & Preferences (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Gives TripSync structured traveller information for matching, group profiling and itinerary planning. |
| **Swipe & Vote (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Gives each member a simple way to express Must Go, Like, Neutral or Skip. |
| **Group Fairness Meter (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Majority voting can repeatedly ignore the same member. The Fairness Meter makes underrepresented preferences visible. |
| **AI Activity Suggestions (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Generates candidate attractions for the group to review before creating the final itinerary. |
| **AI Final Itinerary (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Converts group preferences and voting results into a structured travel plan. |
| **Plan Rescue (Chosen)** | **Kept.** Allows TripSync to remain useful after planning by adjusting affected parts of the itinerary. |
| **Budget Support (Chosen / Simplified)** | **Kept but simplified.** Budget is important, but advanced financial optimisation is outside the current prototype scope. |
| **Live Weather Integration** | **Future Development.** Useful for automatic Plan Rescue, but not required to demonstrate the rescue flow. |
| **Advanced Route Optimisation** | **Future Development.** Combining traffic, opening hours, distance, preferences and time would make the MVP too complex. |
| **Hotel / Flight / Bus Booking** | **Future Development.** Requires external providers and live availability data. |
| **Payment Processing** | **Future Development.** Adds transaction, security and integration requirements outside the current prototype scope. |
| **Travel Marketplace / Merchant Offers** | **Future Development.** Has business potential but is not necessary to validate the current TripSync concept. |
| **Full Social Media / Chat System** | **Dropped from MVP.** TripSync focuses on travel teaming and planning rather than becoming a general social network. |

