## 2.3 Idea Evolution

### Version 1 — AI Travel Planner

The first idea focused mainly on generating an itinerary from:

- Destination
- Budget
- Preferences

**Limitation identified:**  
AI itinerary generation alone did not fully address the challenges of travelling as a group.

---

### Version 2 — Group Travel Planner

We expanded the concept with:

- Group preferences
- Activity voting
- Group matching
- Budget awareness

**Reason for change:**  
We wanted every traveller to participate in decision-making instead of relying on one person to organise the trip.

---

### Version 3 — Adaptive Group Travel Planner

We added:

- Group Fairness Meter
- Plan Rescue
- Adaptive planning
- Budget-aware alternatives

**Reason for change:**  
A useful travel planner should continue helping after the itinerary has already been generated, especially when circumstances change.

---

### Version 4 — Travel Teaming + Group Planning

We expanded TripSync with:

- Open Trips
- Private Groups
- Travel Compatibility
- Travel Buddies
- School / Club Trips
- Company / Team Trips

**Reason for change:**  
We recognised another problem before planning even begins:

> Some users do not have suitable people to travel with.

This led to our current positioning:

> **Find people. Plan together. Travel better.**

### Mentor Consultation

Our team did not conduct a formal mentor consultation during this ideation phase.

The ideation evidence above documents our team's own:

- Brainstorming
- Idea evaluation
- Feature comparison
- Scope decisions
- Prototype iteration

---

# 3. Design & Prototype

## 3.1 UI Prototype

**UI Prototype:**  
[Add Public Prototype Link]

The current TripSync prototype demonstrates the main product structure and planning journey.

---

## 3.2 Open Trip vs Private Group

TripSync separates public travel discovery from private planning.

| **Mode** | **Purpose** | **Access** |
|---|---|---|
| **Open Trip** | Find compatible travel companions | Public discovery |
| **Friends** | Plan with friends | Private |
| **Family** | Plan with family | Private |
| **Couple** | Plan as two people | Private |
| **School / Club** | Plan for a class, club or society | Private |
| **Company / Team** | Plan an outing, team-building trip or retreat | Private |

Open Trips are used when the user still needs travel companions.

Private Groups are used when the group already exists.

---

## 3.3 Trip Creation

The current prototype uses a multi-step trip creation flow.

### Step 1 — Who Are You Travelling With?

Users choose:

- Open Trip
- Friends
- Family
- Couple
- School / Club
- Company / Team

### Step 2 — Trip Details

The current interface supports:

- Trip Name
- State / Region
- Destination
- Trip Dates
- One-day Trip option
- Minimum Budget
- Maximum Budget
- Transport Preference
- Maximum Members
- Travel Style

Travel Style options include:

- Chill
- Food
- Nature
- Shopping
- Photography
- Adventure
- Culture
- Relaxation
- Team Building

### Step 3 — Open Trip Matching or Private Invitations

For an **Open Trip**, users can select matching preferences such as:

- Students
- Young Adults
- Food Lovers
- Photographers
- Adventure Travellers
- Relaxed Travellers
- Budget Travellers

For a **Private Friends Trip**, the prototype includes an Invite People screen with:

- Friends
- Travel Buddies
- Search
- Selectable people

---

## 3.4 Current Planning Flow

The current TripSync planning flow is:

> **Group Lobby → Travel Preferences → Group Profile → Generate Attractions → Vote Together → Voting Progress → Group Match → Generate Final Itinerary → Itinerary → Plan Rescue**

---

### Group Lobby

The Group Lobby is the shared workspace for one trip.

It can display:

- Trip name
- Group member count
- Current members
- Compatibility information
- Planning status
- Invitation actions
- Start / continue planning actions

---

### Travel Personality & Trip Preferences

TripSync uses travel preferences to understand each traveller.

Current preference categories include:

- Travel Style
- Food
- Wake-up Time
- Interests
- Transport Preference
- Budget-related preferences

The prototype also includes a **Group Profile / Group Vibe** screen that combines member preferences into:

- Shared interests
- Compromise points
- AI suggestions

---

### Generate Attractions

Before generating the final itinerary, TripSync generates candidate attractions for the group to review.

Example activities include:

- Genting SkyWorlds
- Awana SkyWay
- Chin Swee Caves Temple
- Skytropolis Indoor Theme Park
- Genting Premium Outlets

This stage is separate from the final itinerary generation.

---

### Vote Together

Members review attractions and vote using:

- ❤️ **Must Go**
- 👍 **Like**
- 😐 **Neutral**
- 👎 **Skip**

The voting interface can show:

- Attraction
- Estimated cost
- Estimated duration
- Tags
- Match score
- Voting progress

---

### Group Match & Fairness

After voting, TripSync presents group-level results.

The Group Match screen can include:

- Overall group match
- Group preference distribution
- Individual representation
- Fairness score
- AI insight

The **Fairness Meter** is designed to highlight when one traveller's preferences are less represented than the rest of the group.

---

### Final Itinerary

TripSync uses a separate AI generation stage to build the final trip plan after the group decision process.

The itinerary can show:

- Trip duration
- Estimated plan cost
- Group match
- Day tabs
- Timeline
- Activities
- Estimated activity cost
- Activity match

This separates:

> **AI Activity Suggestions**

from:

> **AI Final Itinerary Generation**

---

### 🚨 Plan Rescue

Plan Rescue is TripSync's main adaptive feature.

The prototype is designed around six common problems:

- 🌧️ Bad Weather
- ⏰ Running Late
- 💸 Over Budget
- 😴 Too Tired
- 🚫 Place Closed
- 👥 Group Changed

Instead of rebuilding the whole trip, TripSync focuses on the affected part of the plan and proposes an updated itinerary.

---

## 3.5 Main App Areas

TripSync currently uses five main navigation areas.

### Explore

Used for:

- Discovering Open Trips
- Searching for trips
- Starting Open Trip discovery
- Creating a new trip

### My Trips

Used for trips the user has created or joined.

### Plan

Used for continuing the planning process for the selected trip.

### People

Used for travel-related contacts and relationships such as:

- Friends
- Travel Buddies
- Family
- Classmates
- Team Members / Colleagues

### Profile

Used for the current user's travel preferences and personal profile.

---

# 4. What Makes TripSync Different

## 🔎 4.1 Travel Teaming

TripSync is not only about deciding where to go.

It also supports the step before planning:

> **Who should I travel with?**

Open Trips give solo travellers and other users a way to discover potentially compatible travel groups.

---

## ⚖️ 4.2 Group Fairness

Normal majority voting can repeatedly favour the same people.

TripSync therefore includes a **Fairness Meter** to make underrepresented preferences visible during group planning.

Example:

| **Traveller** | **Representation** |
|---|---:|
| Member A | 92% |
| Member B | 81% |
| Member C | 67% |
| Member D | 45% |

If one traveller is significantly underrepresented, TripSync can suggest activities that better match that person's preferences.

---

## 🚨 4.3 Plan Rescue

TripSync is designed to remain useful after the itinerary has already been created.

Instead of starting again when something changes, Plan Rescue focuses on repairing the affected section of the trip.

Example:

**Original Plan**

> 10:00 AM → Outdoor Attraction

**Problem**

> 🌧️ Bad Weather

**Updated Plan**

> 10:00 AM → Nearby Indoor Alternative

Possible factors considered include:

- Group preferences
- Available time
- Budget
- Activity type
- Location

---

## 🎮 4.4 Game-Like Group Formation

TripSync takes inspiration from multiplayer team formation.

Instead of:

> **Find players → Form team → Play**

TripSync uses:

> **Find travellers → Form group → Agree → Travel**

---

